    "tier": 1,
    "description": "<p>A lush mountain shrub crowned by an enormous spectacular flower. Its nectar is restorative, but four powerful vines defend the bloom.</p>\n<section class=\"cybermancy-fast-play\"><h3>FAST PLAY</h3><p><strong><em>Opening:</em></strong> When a creature enters Very Close, raise the four Guardian Vines and become hostile while keeping the flower visibly intact.</p><p><strong><em>Default:</em></strong> Vine Lash intruders; use Entangling Lash when Restraining someone helps protect the flower.</p><p><strong><em>As Vines Fall:</em></strong> Track active vines. At three subdued, Fewer Vines, Fewer Threats reduces attack damage.</p><p><strong><em>Protect the Reward:</em></strong> Telegraph Do Not Cut the Vines: serious damage spoils nectar; non-injurious restraint preserves it.</p><p><strong><em>Resolution:</em></strong> At four subdued vines, stop attacking and allow one dose of Mercy Nectar to be harvested.</p><p><strong><em>Goal:</em></strong> Make the encounter a visible nonlethal puzzle where restraint and teamwork preserve a useful healing reward.</p></section>",
